// RtOp, system: Files, the console, the command line, time, logs, the clipboard, serial ports, processes and random numbers. Read by `compiler/kir/build.rs`.
/// `std.fs` (spec 14.3). The ones that can fail leave their error
/// for `kv_take_error`, like `parse`.
FsReadText,
FsWriteText,
FsAppendText,
FsExists,
FsList,
FsRemove,
FsCreateDir,
/// `std.time`, `std.math`, `std.io`, `std.cli` (spec 14.4–14.6).
TimeNowMs,
TimeMonotonicMs,
TimeSleepMs,
IoReadLine,
CliArgs,
CliExit,
/// `cli.parse<T>()`: the arguments as a tuple of optionals, one per
/// field (`lower_cli.rs`).
CliParse,
TimeWaitUntil,
/// `spawn process f(args)` (spec 9.8, `lower_process.rs`): in the
/// parent's task, the call run in a child (it can fail); in the child,
/// which call it runs, its arguments, and its value or error given
/// back.
ProcessRun,
ProcessSite,
ProcessArgs,
ProcessDone,
ProcessFailed,
FsReadBytes,
FsWriteBytes,
FsWriteDurable,
/// Streamed reads (spec 14.3): opening (which can fail), and the next
/// line or piece, an optional.
FsLines,
FsChunks,
ReaderNext,
/// `uses Fs("folder")` (spec 8.1): file access kept inside the folder
/// until the matching leave; enter gives the depth to go back to.
FsScopeEnter,
FsScopeLeave,
/// `io.is_terminal()`: whether standard output is a terminal (spec 14.6).
IoIsTerminal,
/// `io.write(text)`: text without a line end, shown at once (14.6).
IoWrite,
/// `std.log` (spec 14.12): the `[log]` settings, passed once at the
/// start of `main`; a line at a level.
LogConfigure,
LogWrite,
/// OpenTelemetry export (spec 14.12): the collector, passed once at
/// the start of `main`; an event's level, line and type name.
OtlpConfigure,
OtlpExport,
/// `random_bits()` (spec 14.15): 64 random bits for `std.random`.
RandomBits,
/// `io.colors()`: whether standard output shows colors (spec 14.6).
IoColors,
/// The next item of a reader whose loop header has `try` or `catch`
/// (spec 14.3): a failed read sets an `FsError` instead of panicking.
ReaderTryNext,
/// `io.read_hidden()` (spec 14.6): a line typed unseen.
IoReadHidden,
/// `cli.stop_hold(grace_ms)`, `cli.stop_asked()` and `cli.stop_done(id)`
/// in `std/cli.kav` (decision 0088): holds on the program's stop.
CliStopHold,
CliStopAsked,
CliStopDone,
/// `time.zone_offset(name, ms)` (spec 14.4): seconds ahead of UTC, or
/// `none` for an unknown zone (`runtime/native/src/rt_zone.rs`).
ZoneOffset,
/// `clipboard.read_text()` and `write_text(text)` (spec 14.17);
/// both can fail (`runtime/native/src/rt_clipboard.rs`).
ClipReadText,
ClipWriteText,
/// `env(name)` (spec 10.13): the variable, or an error when it is
/// not set (`runtime/native/src/rt_std.rs`).
EnvGet,
/// A file's details as numbers (for `fs.info` in `std/fs.kav`), its
/// permissions, renaming, copying and removing a folder with its
/// contents (spec 14.3); all can fail (`runtime/native/src/rt_file_info.rs`).
FileInfoStat,
FileInfoSetReadOnly,
FileInfoSetPermissions,
FileInfoRename,
FileInfoCopy,
FileInfoRemoveAll,
/// Serial ports (spec 14.18), by number: the ports there are, open
/// (can fail), read and write (can fail), close
/// (`runtime/native/src/rt_serial.rs`).
SerialPorts,
SerialOpen,
SerialRead,
SerialWrite,
SerialClose,
/// At the start of `main` (spec 10.5): what built the program, between
/// its marks; whether it answers `--version` with it; and the
/// compiler's `RtOp::FINGERPRINT`, which the runtime checks.
CliVersion,
/// `fs.symlink(target, link)` (spec 14.3): a symbolic link; can fail
/// (`runtime/native/src/rt_file_info.rs`).
FileInfoSymlink,
/// `std.window` (spec 14.22), by the window's number: open (title,
/// width, height; can fail), the events as numbers (wait), their texts,
/// the size, the scale, listening to input, the title, full screen,
/// locking the pointer, and close (`runtime/native/src/rt_window.rs`).
WindowOpen,
WindowEvents,
WindowTexts,
WindowSize,
WindowScale,
WindowListen,
WindowTitle,
WindowFullscreen,
WindowLockCursor,
WindowClose,
/// `uses Process("git")` (spec 14.23): while the function runs, only
/// program `a` (owned) may be run; `FsScopeLeave` ends it, as it ends a
/// folder.
ScopeProgram,
/// `std.process` (spec 14.23), by the child's number
/// (`runtime/native/src/rt_run.rs`): start (the program, its arguments,
/// the folder then the environment's names and values; can fail), the
/// next line as its kind and text (waits), the end as code, processor
/// milliseconds and peak bytes (waits), kill, close, and this program's
/// peak memory.
RunStart,
RunNext,
RunExit,
RunKill,
RunClose,
RunPeak,
/// Blocks given to a call (spec 4.8, decision 0107), kept on the task's
/// scope stack (`runtime/native/src/rt_scopes.rs`), each giving the depth
/// `FsScopeLeave` goes back to: a span named `a` (continuing the
/// `traceparent` text `b`, or 0), a `random.seeded` block with seed `a`,
/// and the depth now, which a function holding such blocks goes back to
/// however it ends. Then the current trace's id and `traceparent` text.
ScopeSpan,
ScopeSeeded,
ScopeMark,
ScopeTraceId,
ScopeTraceparent,
/// `log.count`, `log.gauge` and `log.histogram` (spec 14.12): kind `a`,
/// name `b` (owned), value `c` (a `Float`'s bits), kept for the collector.
OtlpMetric,
/// `log.name_span(name)` (spec 14.12): the current span takes name `a`
/// (owned); outside a span, nothing.
ScopeRename,
/// `std.fs`'s `FileWriter` (spec 14.3), by the writer's number
/// (`runtime/native/src/rt_writers.rs`): open path `a` (can fail), write
/// `Bytes` `b` (can fail), finish with sync flag `b` (can fail), and let
/// it go.
FsWriterOpen,
FsWriterWrite,
FsWriterFinish,
FsWriterClose,
